<section class="section">
  <div class="container article-body" style="max-width:920px;">
    
    <h2>What Is the S'mores Blizzard® Treat?</h2>
    <p>The S'mores Blizzard captures the three core campfire flavors — graham cracker, marshmallow, and chocolate — in a cold, creamy format. Graham cracker pieces provide crunch and a slightly sweet grain flavor. Marshmallow topping adds pillowy sweetness. Chocolate fudge delivers the chocolate layer. It is one of the most popular returning seasonals in the DQ Blizzard lineup. Available Summer 2026.</p>
  <p>See all 2026 seasonal and core Blizzards on <a href="/">The Dairy Queen Menu</a>.</p>

    <h2>Why S'mores Works as a Blizzard</h2>
  <p>S'mores is one of the better seasonal Blizzard concepts because all three components work at cold temperatures. Graham cracker pieces hold their crunch. Marshmallow topping distributes well through soft serve without becoming icy. Fudge sauce creates a chocolate depth that ties the flavors together. Compare this to the <a href="/items/dipped-strawberry-cheesecake-blizzard">Dipped Strawberry Cheesecake</a> (more fruity) or the <a href="/items/confetti-cake-blizzard">Confetti Cake</a> (sweeter, more birthday-cake adjacent).</p>
  <h2>Limited Time — Order Before It's Gone</h2>
  <p>The S'mores Blizzard is available for Summer 2026 only. It typically runs from approximately June through late August. Check your local <a href="/locations">DQ location</a> for exact availability.</p>

    <h2>How It Compares to Other Blizzards</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table"><thead><tr><th>Blizzard</th><th>Mini Price</th><th>Small Cal</th><th>Flavor Profile</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>S'mores Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$4.49</td><td>500</td><td>Campfire classic — summer only</td></tr><tr><td>Dipped Strawberry Cheesecake</td><td class="price-cell">$4.49</td><td>540</td><td>Fruity + cheesecake — summer only</td></tr><tr><td>Confetti Cake Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$4.49</td><td>490</td><td>Cake + sprinkles — summer only</td></tr><tr><td>Choco Brownie Extreme</td><td class="price-cell">$3.99</td><td>510</td><td>Year-round chocolate alternative</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

    <h2>Ordering Tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>First timer?</strong> Order a Mini (4.49) — it's 4–5 spoonfuls, perfect for a taste test before committing to a full cup.</li>
      <li><strong>Best size for one person:</strong> Small (5.29) at 500 calories hits the sweet spot of satisfaction without going overboard.</li>
      <li><strong>Upgrade option:</strong> Ask to blend in a hot fudge swirl for richer chocolate depth, or add extra mix-ins (~$0.50).</li>
      <li><strong>Check the flip:</strong> DQ guarantees every Blizzard is thick enough to hold upside down — if your crew doesn't flip it, it's free.</li>
    </ul>

